@H 1167 := "the SUPER-ADDITIVE SURPLUS S(γ)=φ_joint−Σφ_parts PEAKS at the critical A⇄G coupling γ=1.0 — the operational 1+1>2 advantage is MAXIMAL exactly where the engine is critical, and (anti-redundancy) the low-γ rise of S is DECOUPLED from raw φ" :: discovery [🟢 SUPPORTED-NUMERICAL]
  seed       = "MITOSIS-ENGINE cross-arc: H_1158 🟢 showed faithful φ_EI PEAKS at the critical coupling γ=1.0 (inverted-U). Super-additivity (whole − sum of parts = the 1+1>2 surplus) is the ESSENCE of integration. Does the SURPLUS S(γ) — how much the COUPLED whole exceeds its INDEPENDENT sub-parts — ALSO peak at criticality, or is a raw-φ peak NOT a whole−sum surplus peak (since the parts' own φ also moves with γ)? NEW axis: H_1046 synergy was on the PLANNING battery, NOT the γ-criticality sweep."
  method     = "reuse H_1158 simulate_gamma (the A⇄G coupling γ-sweep, FIXED wake envelope) + h1119 phi_stage / faithful_phi (PROVEN ≡ stdlib). Partition the 6-channel system into 2 INDEPENDENT sub-parts P_A={0,1,2} ⊥ P_B={3,4,5}. PRIMARY surplus S(γ)=φ_joint(n=6) − (φ_partA(n=3)+φ_partB(n=3)), SAME median-binarize discretization on each sub-system. SECOND corroborating surplus = Williams-Beer I_min synergy atom of a cross-part triple (T=ch0; sources ch3,ch4), reused VERBATIM from H_1017 _pid_two_source (NO MIP). Sweep SAME γ∈{0,0.15,0.35,0.60,1.00,1.60,2.50} as H_1158, 12 seeds, n=6."
  mirror     = "STEP 0 BEFORE scoring (a_phi_iit4_tool): live `hexa run h1012_ref_faithful.hexa` n=4/5/6 reproduced (|Δ|≤1e-4 vs LIVE stdlib stdout) + h1012.prove_mirrors_at_n n=4 AND n=5 PROVEN; WB synergy validated on XOR(syn>0)/COPY(syn≈0) canonical cases. All PASS."
  F1_interior= "S(γ) INTERIOR argmax at γ=1.00 ✅ (inverted-U, not endpoint) — coincides with the raw-φ peak γ=1.0 AND the WB-synergy peak γ=1.0"
  F2_vs_sub  = "S(peak)−S(γ=0)   Cohen's d = +3.56 ≥ 0.8 ✅"
  F3_vs_super= "S(peak)−S(γ=2.5) Cohen's d = +3.47 ≥ 0.8 ✅"
  result     = "🟢 SUPPORTED — inverted-U surplus: S = −0.0011 (γ0) → −0.0014 (γ0.15) → +0.0117 (γ0.35) → +0.0233 (γ0.60) → ★+0.0294 (γ=1.0)★ → +0.0065 (γ1.6) → 0.0000 (γ2.5 fully locked). ALL THREE gates pass; WB-synergy corroborates (peaks γ=1.0)."
  anti_redund= "S ≠ raw φ — DECOUPLED at low γ: at γ=0 raw φ_joint=+0.0019 but S=−0.0011 (NEGATIVE — at independence the sub-parts already carry the tiny φ, the whole adds nothing/less); at γ=0.15 raw φ_joint jumps 13× to +0.025 while S stays ~0 (−0.0014) — early coupling raises whole AND parts EQUALLY, NO surplus yet. Surplus only turns positive from γ=0.35. So the ARGMAX coincides (both γ=1.0) but the LOW-γ shoulder of S is flat/negative where raw φ is already rising — the result is NOT a re-statement of H_1158."
  finding    = "the super-additive 1+1>2 surplus (how much the coupled whole exceeds its independent parts) is MAXIMAL exactly at the critical A⇄G coupling — and is a STRICTER signature of criticality than raw φ: it stays ≈0 through the early-coupling region where raw φ already climbs, then peaks sharply at γ=1.0 and collapses to EXACTLY 0 at the fully-locked γ=2.5 (no whole, no parts, no surplus). Integration-as-surplus, not just integration-as-φ, tracks the critical point."
  synthesis  = "EXTENDS the criticality triangle (H_1153 σ≈1 branching · H_931 SOC self-tunes · H_1158 faithful φ peaks): the φ-peak is specifically a SUPER-ADDITIVE (whole>parts) peak, not merely a parts-inclusive φ-peak. Distinct from H_1046 (synergy on the PLANNING battery = degenerate always-DOWN bigΦ stand-in); here surplus is measured over the γ-CRITICALITY axis = a different, positive question."
  honest     = "toy n=6 (sub-parts n=3) exact MIP-EI, A⊥G toy dynamics per H_1119/H_1158; γ_x = the toy coupling knob; partition P_A⊥P_B is one natural 3+3 split (not unique). LIVE CORE engine, larger n, alternate partitions and scale all UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope). φ + synergy MEASURED (faithful MIP-EI / exact PID), NOT fabricated; NO perplexity (p7). $0 CPU 0-pod SERIAL wall 55.7s."
